[9.06, "o", "\r\n"]
[9.11, "o", "## Distributed Consensus Protocol Overview\r\n\r\nModern distributed systems rely on state machine replication protocols such as [Raft](https://raft.github.io/) and [Paxos](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paxos_(computer_science)) to guarantee linearizable consistency across unreliable network partitions.\r\n\r\n### Key Protocol Attributes\r\n\r\n| Algorithm   | Leader Model        | Fault Tolerance  | Complexity     |\r\n| ----------- | ------------------- | ---------------- | -------------- |\r\n| Raft        | Strong Leader       | (N-1)/2 failures | Understandable |\r\n| Multi-Paxos | Weak / Multi-Leader | (N-1)/2 failures | High           |\r\n| EPaxos      | Leaderless          | (N-1)/2 failures | Very High      |\r\n\r\nFor more architectural details, refer to the [etcd documentation](https://etcd.io/docs/) and the [MIT 6.824 Distributed Systems course](https://pdos.csail.mit.edu/6.824/).\r\n\r\n"]
